{"cmd":"add","id":"node_package","type":"card","group":"group_platform","data":{"title":"Package Manifest & Dependencies","description":"The package is named latam-geodb-colombia (v1.0.0). It is described as 'LATAM Market Intelligence — Geo DB Colombia (demo Kurian)', which positions it as a client-facing demo of a geographic market-intelligence database for Colombia. It requires Node >= 18. Dependencies:\n- express: HTTP API and static hosting.\n- mysql2: MySQL 8 access with spatial functions.\n- csv-parse: ingests the geodb-v2 CSV datasets.\n- dotenv: local configuration.\nThe only npm script is 'start' (node server.js). Migration, load, acceptance and QA scripts are run manually as `node scripts/*.js`.","tags":["domain:platform","tech:nodejs","tech:npm","integration:mysql","integration:csv"],"sourceFiles":["package.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_data_catalog","type":"group","data":{"label":"Data Catalog, Schema & Loading","icon":"fa-solid fa-database","color":"#F2F3F4","borderColor":"#5D6D7E"}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_ui_pages","type":"group","data":{"label":"Market Intelligence UI Pages","icon":"fa-solid fa-desktop","color":"#FDEDEC","borderColor":"#C0392B"}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_env_config","type":"card","group":"group_platform","data":{"title":"Environment Configuration Contract","description":"This file defines how the app connects to its MySQL database. The workspace runtime injects DATABASE_URL, DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_NAME and PORT, and these values always override .env. The example DSN targets the geodb_colombia schema. Security rule: real credentials must never be committed to .env. The QA probe (probe-boot.js) reads the discrete DB_* variables directly, while the app pool (db/pool) is shared by all scripts.","tags":["domain:platform","tech:config","integration:mysql","security:secrets"],"sourceFiles":[".env.example","scripts/probe-boot.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_page_acceptance","type":"card","group":"group_frontend_shell","data":{"title":"Page: Panel de aceptación (acceptance_panel)","description":"Data-quality acceptance dashboard for data stewards and for client sign-off. It shows the list of acceptance checks with pass/fail status and the axis test (coordinate orientation of the geodata). It also shows exceptions, missing sources, the validity of department polygons and the latest load batch with its error and info issue counts. An overall all_green flag tells whether the dataset is accepted. From this page users can re-run validation (POST /v1/validate) or fully reload the CSVs (POST /v1/load), and drill into issues (GET /v1/issues).","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-steward","role:client-reviewer","entity:load-batch","entity:validation-issue","entity:acceptance-check","flow:acceptance-review"],"sourceFiles":["public/index.html","routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"note_project_overview","type":"note","data":{"text":"**LATAM Market Intelligence — Geo DB Colombia (demo Kurian / think4ever)**\n\nA geo-referenced market-intelligence database for Colombia that answers: *where are the professionals (personas) a B2B/tech product could sell to or hire, how many companies/micro-businesses exist per territory, how strong is the education pipeline, and what tech-ecosystem signals exist?*\n\n**Layers:** Department (DIVIPOLA 2-digit) → Municipality (5-digit) → Zone (Bogotá localidades BOG-xx / Medellín comunas MED-xx) → UPZ (Bogotá).\n**Stack:** Node/Express + MySQL (mysql2, spatial POINTs, axis-order long-lat), CSV ingestion via csv-parse, vanilla-JS SPA with Leaflet maps, Spanish (es-CO) UI.\n**Pages:** Mapa, Comparar, Panel de aceptación, Explorador de tablas.\n**Sources:** DANE (GEIH 2025, EMICRON 2024, EM 2021), MEN (enrolment, SNIES), ICFES Saber 11, RUES chambers, SECOP, GitHub Innovation Graph, Meetup, magnet.co-like job boards.\n**Config:** DATABASE_URL / DB_HOST… / PORT injected by workspace runtime.","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/meta_sources.csv","public/js/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_db_pool","type":"card","group":"group_data_store","data":{"title":"db/pool — MySQL Connection Pool","description":"Shared mysql2 promise pool used by the v1 routes and the lib services. It is configured from DATABASE_URL or the DB_HOST/DB_PORT/DB_USER/DB_PASSWORD/DB_NAME variables injected by the workspace runtime, and those injected values always override .env. The default database is geodb_colombia.","tags":["tech:mysql","tech:mysql2","integration:database","tech:dotenv"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js",".env.example"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_page_table_explorer","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Table Explorer Page (table_explorer)","description":"Route shim for the raw data browser (window.T4ETableExplorer from js/table_explorer.js). Business purpose: lets analysts inspect any warehouse table (geo, fact, meta) row-by-row with its provenance from meta_sources—transparency and ad-hoc exploration behind the map and comparison insights.","tags":["domain:data-exploration","role:analyst","role:data-engineer","flow:table-browsing","entity:meta_sources"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/pages/table_explorer.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_health","type":"api","group":"group_platform","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/health (alias /api/health)","description":"Operational health check used by the runtime, smoke tests and operators. It returns the result of mapData.getHealth(), which includes at least status, mysql_version and axis_check_ok. axis_check_ok verifies that spatial points are stored with correct lat/lon axis order: Bogotá 11001 must resolve to about lat 4.6, lon -74.1. Smoke tests additionally require MySQL >= 8.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ status:'ok', mysql_version, axis_check_ok:true, ... } — 503 with same shape when status != 'ok'"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["server.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/check-map.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_data_dictionary","type":"card","group":"group_data_catalog","data":{"title":"Data Dictionary — Geo DB Colombia v2 (diccionario.md)","description":"Human-readable catalogue (Spanish/English) of every table in the Colombian geospatial market-intelligence database v2. It states the core business rule of the whole dataset: the geographic key is DIVIPOLA (2-digit department code, 5-digit municipality code) plus zone_id for intra-city zones of Bogotá (localidades) and Medellín (comunas/corregimientos), and that ALL data is aggregated (no individual-level records, protecting respondent privacy). For each table it documents purpose, official source (DANE, MinSalud, MEN, SNIES, RUES, SECOP II, ICFES, GitHub Innovation Graph, Meetup, Servicio Público de Empleo), the extraction script, row count and column types. Version 2 (5-Oct-2026) added department polygons, public IT procurement, Saber 11 scores, job vacancies, Bogotá Encuesta Multipropósito 2021 layers, developer communities and tech events. It is the reference analysts use to interpret indicators shown in the map, compare and table explorer pages.","tags":["domain:data-catalog","domain:market-intelligence","entity:meta_sources","role:analyst","role:developer","integration:dane","integration:datos.gov.co","tech:markdown"],"sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_map","type":"group","data":{"label":"Geo Market Map & Place Comparison","icon":"fa-solid fa-map-location-dot","color":"#E8F6EF","borderColor":"#1E8E5A","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-map.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/check-map-view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_loader","type":"card","group":"group_ingestion","data":{"title":"CSV Loader (lib/loader.js)","description":"Loads the curated geodb-v2 CSV dataset (data/geodb-v2/csv) for Colombia into MySQL 8 in a single transaction, replacing the previous data set. It turns open-data extracts (DANE, ICFES, SECOP II, Encuesta Multipropósito, chambers of commerce, Meetup, job boards) into a joinable geographic market-intelligence database keyed on DIVIPOLA codes. Business rules: codes are always kept as strings so leading zeros survive (csv-parse cast off); municipality points are built with ST_GeomFromText('POINT(lon lat)', 4326, 'axis-order=long-lat'); only Bogotá (11001) zones get polygons because Medellín comunas geometries are licensed non-commercial (code + name only); Nuevo Belén de Bajirá (27493) is loaded without a point (approved exception); department shapes are validated with ST_GeomFromGeoJSON; department centroid points are the average of their municipalities' points; meta_sources gets a year for every table (META_YEARS seed) plus 8 v2 table registrations from diccionario.md. All CSVs are parsed before touching the DB so a bad file fails early; row counts inserted must equal CSV rows or the whole load rolls back. Load tracking happens in load_batch (running → failed / later validated|failed by validation). After commit it invokes the validation hook (lib/validation.js validateBatch) and tolerates its absence. Exports loadAll({csvDir, log}) → {batchId, rowsLoaded, report[], validation}, TABLE_ORDER, META_YEARS. Operator/admin-only (CLI or admin action), no user input reaches SQL other than CSV values bound as parameters; table names are from a fixed whitelist.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","role:data-admin","entity:load_batch","entity:meta_sources","entity:geo_municipality","entity:geo_zone","flow:data-load","tech:mysql-spatial","tech:csv-parse","integration:filesystem","integration:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_app_js","type":"card","group":"group_frontend_shell","data":{"title":"js/app.js — Client Router & Page Loader","description":"Client-side script referenced by index.html. It provides the global load_page(page) function used by the sidebar links. It is assumed to inject page markup and CSS into #page-main and #page-css, highlight the active nav item by data-page, and handle the #theme-toggle light/dark switch. It is the single entry point that calls both backend API families. The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from index.html.","tags":["domain:frontend","tech:javascript","flow:navigation"],"sourceFiles":["public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_geo_department","type":"table","group":"group_geo_model","data":{"name":"geo_department","columns":[{"name":"department_code","type":"VARCHAR (DIVIPOLA)","pk":true},{"name":"name","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"point","type":"POINT SRID 4326"}],"description":"Colombian departments (DIVIPOLA). Point computed as average of municipality points. Referenced by most department-level fact tables.","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js","lib/compare.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_schema_overview","type":"card","group":"group_db_infra","data":{"title":"Warehouse Schema (db/schema.sql)","description":"MySQL 8 star-like schema for a LATAM market-intelligence demo (Kurian) focused on Colombia: geographic dimension tables (geo_*) keyed by DIVIPOLA codes plus thematic fact tables (fact_*) covering buyer personas from GEIH 2025, education, businesses, public procurement, job vacancies, the developer ecosystem and Bogotá's EM2021 survey, plus meta/load/validation tables for data governance. Translated from a Postgres original (data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql + diccionario.md); CSV headers are authoritative so column names stay untranslated. Rules: DIVIPOLA codes stored as VARCHAR to preserve leading zeros (e.g., '05' Antioquia, '05001' Medellín); spatial columns use SRID 4326 and must be loaded with ST_GeomFromText(wkt, 4326, 'axis-order=long-lat'). The script is idempotent: disables FK checks, drops all 26 tables children-first, and recreates them. Only one hard FK exists (validation_issue→load_batch); other relationships to geo tables are logical and verified by the validation pipeline (unjoined_code issues). All tables InnoDB utf8mb4_unicode_ci.","tags":["domain:data-warehouse","tech:mysql8","tech:spatial-srid-4326","entity:divipola","flow:schema-reset"],"sourceFiles":["db/schema.sql"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_map_departments","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"api/map/departments","description":"GeoJSON FeatureCollection of department polygons with properties {department_code, name, values{indicatorKey: number}} plus indicators[] {key,label,table,column,unit} and attribution[]. Optional persona filter narrows persona indicators. Feeds the Departamentos choropleth.","params":[{"name":"persona","type":"string","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ type:'FeatureCollection', features[], indicators[], attribution[] }"},"auth":"none (read-only, served behind workspace proxy)","sourceFiles":["public/js/map_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_postgres_schema","type":"card","group":"group_data_catalog","data":{"title":"PostgreSQL + PostGIS Schema (schema_postgres.sql)","description":"Portable DDL export of the geo database (header says 'Think4Ever, base geoespacial de Colombia v1', extended with a v2 section dated 2026-10-05 for 'parts 8 and 9'). Enables the PostGIS extension and creates 25 tables: geo tables use geometry(Point,4326) for municipalities and geometry(MultiPolygon,4326) for Bogotá zones and department shapes, with GiST spatial indexes on geo_municipality and geo_zone. Counts are bigint, percentages/means double precision, codes text (preserving leading zeros of DIVIPOLA). No primary keys or foreign keys are declared — relationships are logical via department_code, municipality_code, zone_id. Note: the running app (package.json) uses MySQL via mysql2 and csv-parse, so this file is an alternate/export target for downstream GIS users, while the CSVs are the shared source of truth.","tags":["domain:data-catalog","tech:postgresql","tech:postgis","tech:sql","integration:csv","entity:geo_department","entity:geo_municipality","entity:geo_zone","role:developer","role:data-engineer"],"sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_map_router","type":"card","group":"group_geo_analytics","data":{"title":"routes/map.js — Read-only Map API Router","description":"Express router that implements the business rule 'rule_map_api_readonly'. The public map API exposes only GET endpoints and only aggregated indicators, never individual or personal records. It delegates to lib/mapData for map layers and personas, and to lib/compare for place comparison. A shared wrap() helper serialises results as JSON. Errors become {error: message} with e.status, or 500 by default, so the library layer can raise 400/404 for invalid levels or ids. The router has no authentication and no write paths, which makes it safe for public demos.","tags":["domain:geo-analytics","tech:express","role:analyst","role:guest","entity:department","entity:municipality","entity:localidad","entity:persona","rule:read-only","rule:aggregates-only"],"sourceFiles":["routes/map.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_geo_municipality","type":"table","group":"group_geo_model","data":{"name":"geo_municipality","columns":[{"name":"municipality_code","type":"VARCHAR (DIVIPOLA 5)","pk":true},{"name":"department_code","type":"VARCHAR","fk":"geo_department.department_code"},{"name":"name","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"lat","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"lon","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"wkt","type":"TEXT"},{"name":"point","type":"POINT SRID 4326"}],"description":"1,123 municipalities with long-lat point. 27493 Nuevo Belén de Bajirá has no point (approved exception). Bogotá 11001 is the axis-order test record.","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js","lib/acceptance.js","lib/mapData.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_data_load","type":"note","group":"group_ingest","data":{"text":"**Flow: Dataset Refresh**\n1. `node scripts/migrate.js` checks MySQL >= 8 (no MariaDB), rebuilds the schema, and verifies DIVIPOLA columns are VARCHAR.\n2. `node scripts/load.js` creates a load_batch and loads the geodb-v2 CSVs in TABLE_ORDER, then prints per-table counts and the Bogotá axis check.\n3. `node scripts/acceptance.js [batchId]` validates the batch and sets load_batch.status.\n4. The service is started or restarted, and `scripts/probe-boot.js` / `smoke.js` verify it.\n\n**Role:** data engineer / operator\n**Failure:** any step exits 1; a load failure reports the batch id.","color":"#FEF5E7","sourceFiles":["scripts/migrate.js","scripts/load.js","scripts/acceptance.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_map_municipalities","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"api/map/municipalities","description":"Municipalities with lat/lon, has_event flag and indicator values (persona metro, chamber companies, schools, higher ed, communities, events) for the Ciudades circle layer.","params":[{"name":"persona","type":"string","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ municipalities[{municipality_code,name,lat,lon,has_event,values{}}], indicators[], attribution[] }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/map_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_schema_reset_load","type":"note","group":"group_db_infra","data":{"text":"**Flow: Schema Reset & Data Load**\n1. Operator runs db/schema.sql (FK checks off → DROP 26 tables children-first → FK checks on → CREATE)\n2. Loader (csv-parse) opens a load_batch row with status='running' and source_file\n3. CSV rows inserted via the pool (no multi-statements); geometry built with ST_GeomFromText(wkt, 4326, 'axis-order=long-lat'), department shapes validated with ST_GeomFromGeoJSON\n4. Validators check DIVIPOLA joins, row counts, totals and source coverage; each problem written to validation_issue (error or info)\n5. Batch finalised: status='validated' (no errors) or 'failed'; rows_loaded, finished_at, notes set\n6. meta_sources filled from seeds (description, source, year)\n\n**Roles:** Data engineer / operator\n**Rules:** codes as VARCHAR, SRID 4326 long-lat axis order, idempotent reruns\n**Errors:** failed batch keeps issues for audit; deleting a batch cascades its issues","color":"#ddf4ff","sourceFiles":["db/schema.sql","db/pool.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_load_postgis","type":"note","group":"group_data_catalog","data":{"text":"**Flow: Loading the Geo DB into PostgreSQL/PostGIS**\n1. Run schema_postgres.sql (CREATE EXTENSION postgis; CREATE TABLE x25)\n2. For each table: \\copy <table> FROM csv/<table>.csv (CSV HEADER)\n3. Geo point/zone tables: load wkt into a text column, then SET geom = ST_GeomFromText(wkt, 4326)\n4. geo_department_shape: load geojson as text, then SET geom = ST_Multi(ST_SetSRID(ST_GeomFromGeoJSON(geojson), 4326))\n5. GiST indexes on geo_municipality.geom and geo_zone.geom enable spatial queries\n\n**Roles:** Data engineer / GIS analyst\n**Rules:** SRID 4326 (WGS84); codes kept as text to preserve leading zeros; all data aggregated\n**Edge cases:** Nuevo Belén de Bajirá (2022) has no point; Medellín zones have no geometry (code + name only); 'Rest of the country' rows have NULL municipality_code; BOG-00 = company with no localidad recorded","color":"#F2F3F4","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_map_localidades","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"api/map/localidades","description":"GeoJSON of Bogotá localidades (zone_id) with EM 2021 and company-zone indicators. Not persona-aware.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ features[{properties:{zone_id,name,values{}}}], indicators[], attribution[] }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/map_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_meta_sources","type":"table","group":"group_data_store","data":{"name":"meta_sources","columns":[{"name":"table_name","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"source","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"year","type":"INT"}],"description":"Provenance catalogue that records the origin source and reference year for each data table. The Table Explorer displays it so every aggregate is traceable. Missing entries are likely surfaced as missing_sources in acceptance. The column list is inferred.","sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_personas","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"api/personas","description":"List of the 13 personas (from fact_persona_profile) with ring, used to populate persona filters in Map and Compare.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ personas[{persona, ring}] }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/map_view.js","public/js/compare_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"note_geo_key_rules","type":"note","group":"group_geo_reference","data":{"text":"**Business rules: geographic keys**\n- department_code: DIVIPOLA 2 digits (33 rows incl. Bogotá D.C.)\n- municipality_code: DIVIPOLA 5 digits (first 2 = department)\n- zone_id: intra-city zones, e.g. BOG-xx (Bogotá localidades), Medellín comunas/corregimientos; BOG-00 = unknown localidad\n- Chambers of commerce mapped to their seat municipality (own mapping)\n- Metro areas keyed by the capital's municipality_code; 'Rest of the country' has no code\n- Higher-ed online programmes are counted at the institution HQ → use students_on_campus for local presence\n- Everything is aggregated; no personal data","color":"#E8F6F3","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_compare_places","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"api/compare/places","description":"Selectable places for a compare level with code and parent name.","params":[{"name":"level","type":"string","required":true}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ count, places[{id,name,code,parent}] }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/compare_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_geo_zone_ref","type":"card","group":"group_geo_reference","data":{"title":"geo_zone (Bogotá localidades & Medellín comunas)","description":"Intra-city zone dimension referenced by fact_companies_zone and fact_em2021_localidad via zone_id (BOG-01..BOG-20, BOG-00 = no localidad recorded; MED-01..MED-90 comunas and corregimientos). Bogotá zones carry polygon boundaries (Catastro Bogotá) and power the 'Bogotá por localidad' map layer and the 'localidad' compare level; Medellín zones are code+name only so cannot be drawn. Defined in meta_sources (CSV not in this file batch).","tags":["domain:geography","entity:zone","tech:mysql-spatial"],"sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/meta_sources.csv","data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_companies_zone.csv","public/js/map_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_acceptance","type":"card","group":"group_quality","data":{"title":"Acceptance Checks Engine (lib/acceptance.js)","description":"Read-only engine that computes every acceptance check that determines whether a loaded data set can be trusted and published (rule_acceptance_totals, rule_tolerances, rule_axis_order, rule_approved_exceptions). Each check returns expected / actual / difference / tolerance / ok, plus sub-checks. v1 checks: 1,123 municipalities; 41 urban zones (20 Bogotá with polygon, 21 Medellín without geometry); 11,111 schools; 1,732,523 students grades 9–11; 2,561,707 higher-ed enrolment; 13 personas totalling 1,716,675 employed; 465,498 Bogotá companies and 109,703 Medellín companies; 5,262,313 micro-businesses (±25); per-persona sums across metro/department/segment tables within ±30 of the profile total; zero unjoined codes across 19 JOIN_RULES (fact code → geo table) excluding approved exceptions. v2 checks: 33 valid department polygons (POLYGON type, SRID 4326, matching geo_department), UPZ and further geographic integrity. Also runs the Bogotá axis test (point must be lat 4.31 / lon -74.18 ±0.01 to detect swapped axes), lists approved 'sin geografía' exceptions (Rest of the country, BOG-00, Medellín no geometry, 27493 no point, UPZ without polygon), flags geo/fact tables missing source or year in meta_sources, and returns latest load_batch id. Exports computeAcceptance() and latestBatchId(); persistence is delegated to validation.js.","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-admin","role:analyst","entity:validation_check","entity:geo_municipality","entity:fact_persona_profile","flow:validation","tech:mysql-spatial","integration:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["lib/acceptance.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_geo_department_shape","type":"table","group":"group_geo_model","data":{"name":"geo_department_shape","columns":[{"name":"department_code","type":"VARCHAR","pk":true,"fk":"geo_department.department_code"},{"name":"name","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"geojson","type":"LONGTEXT"}],"description":"Department boundary polygons (DANE Marco Geoestadístico 2018, WGS84) stored as GeoJSON text; 33 must be valid POLYGON SRID 4326. Drives department choropleth.","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js","lib/acceptance.js","lib/mapData.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_compare","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"api/compare","description":"Compares 2-4 places of one level and returns aligned indicator values with source/year. Errors return non-2xx with {error} (e.g. invalid level, fewer than 2 ids, mixed levels).","params":[{"name":"level","type":"department|municipality|localidad","required":true},{"name":"ids","type":"comma-separated codes","required":true},{"name":"persona","type":"string","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ level, level_label, places[{id,name,code,parent}], indicators[{label,table,unit,values[],source{source_name,year}}], note, persona_note? }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/compare_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_geo_zone","type":"table","group":"group_geo_model","data":{"name":"geo_zone","columns":[{"name":"zone_id","type":"VARCHAR (BOG-xx / MED-xx)","pk":true},{"name":"municipality_code","type":"VARCHAR","fk":"geo_municipality.municipality_code"},{"name":"zone_type","type":"VARCHAR (localidad, comuna...)"},{"name":"zone_code","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"name","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"lat","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"lon","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"geojson","type":"LONGTEXT"},{"name":"wkt","type":"LONGTEXT"},{"name":"geometry","type":"GEOMETRY SRID 4326"}],"description":"41 urban zones: 20 Bogotá localidades with polygon, 21 Medellín comunas/corregimientos without geometry due to non-commercial license. BOG-00 (Sin localidad) intentionally absent.","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js","lib/acceptance.js","lib/mapData.js","lib/compare.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_validation","type":"card","group":"group_quality","data":{"title":"Batch Validation Service (lib/validation.js)","description":"Implements flow_validation: takes a load_batch (given id or latest), runs computeAcceptance(), and converts the results into persisted validation_issue rows so data quality is auditable per batch. Failed checks become 'error' issues typed count_mismatch (municipalities, zones, upz, department_polygons) or total_mismatch (other totals); each unjoined code becomes an unjoined_code error (capped at 50 per column); a wrong Bogotá axis becomes an error tagged rule_axis_order; tables without source/year become missing_source errors; approved exceptions are written as severity 'info' no_geography_exception. Within a transaction it deletes prior issues for the batch, inserts the new ones and sets load_batch.status to 'validated' only if acceptance passed and zero errors, otherwise 'failed', with a summary note (passed/total, axis OK/FALLA, errors, approved exceptions). Triggered automatically after loads and manually by the 'Revalidar' button. Exports validateBatch and run alias. Errors: no batch, batch not found, DB failure → rollback.","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-admin","entity:validation_issue","entity:load_batch","flow:validation","flow:revalidate","integration:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["lib/validation.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_persona_profile","type":"table","group":"group_geo_model","data":{"name":"fact_persona_profile","columns":[{"name":"persona","type":"VARCHAR","pk":true},{"name":"ring","type":"VARCHAR (core, ...)"},{"name":"employed","type":"INT"}],"description":"The 13 tech-talent personas (total 1,716,675 employed); ring='core' defines core IT. Parent for persona breakdowns in fact_persona_metro, fact_persona_department, fact_persona_segment (sums must match within ±30).","sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js","lib/acceptance.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_lib_mapdata","type":"card","group":"group_geo_analytics","data":{"title":"lib/mapData — Map Aggregation Service","description":"Domain service behind the map endpoints. It queries MySQL for geography (departments, municipalities, Bogotá localidades) joined with aggregated indicators and applies persona-based segment logic. It provides getDepartments, getMunicipalities, getLocalidades and getPersonas. It enforces that only aggregates leave the system. The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from routes/map.js.","tags":["domain:geo-analytics","entity:department","entity:municipality","entity:localidad","entity:persona","tech:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["routes/map.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_map_view_frontend","type":"card","group":"group_map","data":{"title":"Mapa Page (map_view) Frontend Contract","description":"This is the analyst-facing Leaflet map page, made of public/js/map_view.js, a page shim and pages/map_view.html. It calls the department, municipality, localidad and personas APIs using relative URLs only; absolute '/...' fetches are forbidden because of the proxy prefix. Choropleth classes are computed as quintiles (computeQuintiles/classOf) on the brand ramp #E9EEF7 → #11255A. Null values show as no-data #DDDDDD and the text 'n.a.'. The page uses tooltips, fitBounds and invalidateSize. Clicking a place renders a place-card; the prompt 'Haga clic en un lugar del mapa' appears until one is selected. A link jumps to compare_view. Accessibility requirements: the layer selector has role=radiogroup and the detail panel has aria-live=polite. The UI copy is in Spanish (es-CO number formatting).","tags":["domain:geo-map","tech:leaflet","tech:frontend","role:market-analyst","flow:map-exploration","a11y"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/check-map-view.js","scripts/smoke.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_acceptance_panel","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Panel de aceptación — data acceptance QA (acceptance_panel.js)","description":"Quality gate for the data owner/demo reviewer to decide whether the latest load_batch is accepted. Shows a verdict (passed/total checks, all_green), stat cards, a totals table grouped into v1 'Totales de carga' (row totals per table vs expected with tolerance) and v2 'Integridad geográfica' (sub-checks such as max deviation per persona, unmatched codes), the Bogotá axis-order test (ST_Latitude/ST_Longitude of 11001 must be ≈ lat 4.31 lon -74.18, SRID shown), latest batch details (rows loaded, errors, info exceptions, duration, previous batch, notes) and issues split into blocking errors vs approved 'sin geografía' info exceptions (which do not block acceptance). Also verifies every table has source/year in meta_sources. 'Revalidar' POSTs v1/validate, disables the button while running, announces progress via an aria-live region and refreshes. Dates shown in America/Bogota (COT).","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-owner","role:admin","flow:acceptance-validation","entity:load_batch","entity:issue","tech:mysql-spatial"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/acceptance_panel.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_lib_compare","type":"card","group":"group_geo_analytics","data":{"title":"lib/compare — Place Comparison Service","description":"Domain service that lists comparable places per level (listPlaces) and builds multi-place indicator comparisons, optionally through a persona lens (compare). It validates the level and ids parameters and throws errors that carry an HTTP status. The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from routes/map.js.","tags":["domain:geo-analytics","entity:place","entity:persona","flow:market-comparison"],"sourceFiles":["routes/map.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_persona_department","type":"table","group":"group_persona_labor","data":{"name":"fact_persona_department","columns":[{"name":"persona","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"department_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"department","type":"text"},{"name":"employed","type":"bigint"}],"description":"Employed people per persona by department (GEIH 2025), 411 rows. Main choropleth source for 'where are my personas' department maps and department comparisons.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_map_explore","type":"note","group":"group_map","data":{"text":"**Flow: Market Map Exploration**\n1. The analyst opens '/'. index.html shows a sidebar linking map_view, compare_view and table_explorer.\n2. map_view loads /api/map/departments and renders a quintile choropleth (5-step navy ramp, grey for no data).\n3. The analyst switches the layer (radiogroup): departments → municipalities (points, event markers) → Bogotá localidades.\n4. Optional: the analyst picks a persona from /api/personas, and department values are recomputed for that talent pool.\n5. Hovering shows a tooltip. Clicking renders a place-card with indicators, each with its source and year.\n6. The analyst can jump to compare_view.\n\n**Rules:** every indicator shows source and year; 27493 is never mapped; [lon,lat] GeoJSON order; nulls display as 'n.a.'\n**Roles:** market analyst / sales (Kurian demo audience)","color":"#E8F6EF","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-map-view.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/check-map.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_map_exploration","type":"note","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"text":"**Flow: Explore a market indicator on the map**\n1. Analyst opens Mapa; loading overlay shown until geo layers load\n2. Picks a layer (radio list; shows friendly name + raw table/column)\n3. Optionally filters by persona (13 personas); note warns on low-reliability/limited coverage\n4. Map renders departments as choropleth (5 quantile-like classes, grey = no data) or cities as proportional circles; event cities get orange ring\n5. Top overlay shows layer title/unit; geo-note warns if layer is partial (e.g. EMICRON 25 depts, Medellín zones w/o shapes)\n6. Analyst clicks or jumps to a place → place card lists indicators, raw names, events, and actions (e.g. add to compare)\n\n**Data:** geo_department_shape, geo_municipality, fact_* tables\n**Rules:** missing ≠ zero; aggregated data only","color":"#FDEDEC","sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/map_view.css","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_persona_metro","type":"table","group":"group_persona_labor","data":{"name":"fact_persona_metro","columns":[{"name":"persona","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"municipality_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"metro_area","type":"text"},{"name":"employed","type":"bigint"}],"description":"Employed people per persona by metropolitan area of the capital cities (GEIH 2025); municipality_code is the capital's code; 'Rest of the country' row has NULL code (non-geo row). 379 rows. Feeds city-circle sizing on the map when a persona is selected.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_compare","type":"note","group":"group_map","data":{"text":"**Flow: Place Comparison**\n1. The analyst picks a level (department / municipality / localidad).\n2. GET /api/compare/places?level=… populates the selectors.\n3. The analyst selects 2 or more places.\n4. GET /api/compare?level=…&ids=a,b returns an indicator × place matrix with source and year per row.\n5. The UI renders a table-navy grid; nulls display as 'n.a.'.\n\n**Errors:** 400 when fewer than 2 ids, ids mix levels (e.g. 11 + 11001), or the level is unknown.","color":"#E8F6EF","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-map.js","scripts/smoke.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_validation","type":"note","group":"group_quality","data":{"text":"**Flow: Validation / Revalidar**\n1. Trigger: loader post-load hook (evt_post_load_validation) or user clicks 'Revalidar' on Panel de aceptación\n2. Resolve batch id (argument or MAX(load_batch.id))\n3. computeAcceptance(): v1 totals, persona sums (±30), unjoined codes (19 join rules minus exceptions), v2 polygons/UPZ, axis test (Bogotá 4.31 / -74.18 ±0.01), exceptions list, missing meta_sources\n4. Map failures → validation_issue errors (count_mismatch, total_mismatch, unjoined_code ≤50/column, missing_source); exceptions → info rows\n5. TX: DELETE old issues for batch, INSERT new, UPDATE load_batch.status = validated | failed + note\n6. Panel renders verdict, totals table, axis card, batch status, issue lists\n\n**Rules:** validated only if accepted AND 0 errors; approved exceptions never count as errors\n**Approved exceptions:** 'Rest of the country' (no municipality), BOG-00 Sin localidad, Medellín comunas without geometry (non-commercial license), 27493 Nuevo Belén de Bajirá without point, Bogotá UPZ without polygon","color":"#e8f8ee","sourceFiles":["lib/validation.js","lib/acceptance.js","public/pages/acceptance_panel.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_market_comparison","type":"note","group":"group_geo_analytics","data":{"text":"**Flow: Market Comparison**\n1. Analyst opens Comparar (compare_view).\n2. Analyst chooses a level and the app calls GET /api/compare/places?level=… to list the candidates.\n3. Analyst selects several places and optionally a persona.\n4. App calls GET /api/compare?level=…&ids=…&persona=… and renders a side-by-side indicator table or chart.\n\n**Roles:** Analyst\n**Rules:** all places must share one level; read-only access\n**Errors:** invalid level or ids → 4xx { error } raised by lib/compare","color":"#d5f5e3","sourceFiles":["routes/map.js","public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_ingest","type":"group","data":{"label":"Data Ingestion & Schema Management","icon":"fa-solid fa-database","color":"#FEF5E7","borderColor":"#C7820A","sourceFiles":["scripts/migrate.js","scripts/load.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_persona_segment","type":"table","group":"group_persona_labor","data":{"name":"fact_persona_segment","columns":[{"name":"persona","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"municipality_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"city","type":"text"},{"name":"buyer_type","type":"text"},{"name":"employed","type":"bigint"},{"name":"interviews","type":"bigint"}],"description":"Direct cross-tab persona × city × buyer_type ('who buys' — e.g. private firm, government, self-employed). Supports go-to-market segmentation: which sales channel reaches each persona in each city. interviews flags small-sample cells. 346 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"note_business_rules_exceptions","type":"note","group":"group_quality","data":{"text":"**Business rules — geography & data integrity**\n- rule_axis_order: all points/polygons in WGS84 SRID 4326, long-lat; Bogotá test point verifies axis order\n- rule_acceptance_totals / rule_tolerances: fixed expected totals; exact unless tolerance (micro ±25, persona sums ±30 per persona)\n- rule_approved_exceptions: rows/tables 'sin geografía' are flagged, kept out of Map and Compare, logged as info\n- rule_source_year_required: every table must have source + year in meta_sources or it is not published\n- Licensing: Medellín comunas geometry not stored (non-commercial license)\n- Privacy: all figures are aggregates; no personal data","color":"#fff8e1","sourceFiles":["lib/acceptance.js","lib/tables.js","lib/loader.js","public/pages/table_explorer.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_migrate","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"Schema Migration CLI (scripts/migrate.js)","description":"This script idempotently rebuilds the geodb_colombia schema from db/schema.sql. The schema uses DROP IF EXISTS + CREATE. The script strips '--' comment lines and executes statements one at a time; on failure it logs the first 300 characters of the failing statement.\nPreconditions: MySQL >= 8.0 is required and MariaDB is rejected, because the schema needs POINT SRID 4326 columns and the axis-order option.\nAfter migrating, it lists all tables. It then enforces a key business rule: all DIVIPOLA code columns must be VARCHAR so leading zeros survive (e.g. '05' Antioquia, '05001' Medellín). Those columns are department_code, municipality_code, seat_municipality_code, zone_id, zone_code and localidad_code; if any is not VARCHAR, the migration fails.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","tech:mysql8","tech:cli","role:data-engineer","entity:divipola-code","rule:varchar-codes"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/migrate.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_v1_router","type":"card","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"title":"routes/v1.js — Data Quality & Acceptance API","description":"Express router for the 'Panel de aceptación' and the 'Explorador de tablas'. It lets data stewards and client reviewers verify that the 27 source CSVs were loaded correctly into Geo DB Colombia and accept the dataset. It exposes read endpoints for acceptance checks, the latest batch, issues and table browsing. It also exposes two write operations: re-validate and full reload. A module-level 'busy' mutex permits only one write at a time, and a concurrent call gets 409 'Operación en curso: <op>'. The mutex lives in process memory, so it is not shared across multiple Node instances. Errors are logged with the [v1] prefix and returned as {error} with e.status or 500. There is no authentication even on the destructive POST /v1/load, which is a security consideration if the app is exposed beyond a demo.","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-steward","role:client-reviewer","entity:load-batch","entity:validation-issue","tech:express","tech:mysql","rule:single-writer","security:no-auth"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_ict_by_sector","type":"table","group":"group_persona_labor","data":{"name":"fact_ict_by_sector","columns":[{"name":"sector","type":"text","pk":true},{"name":"employed","type":"bigint"},{"name":"share_pct","type":"double precision"}],"description":"Distribution of IT staff (the 4 core personas) by the employer's industry, GEIH 2025. Non-geographic (national); shows that much IT talent sits outside the tech sector, informing vertical targeting. 12 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_latest_batch_helper","type":"card","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"title":"latestBatch() — Batch Status Summary","description":"Internal helper that builds the status summary of the most recent ETL run. It reads the newest load_batch (id, country_code, source_file, status, rows_loaded, started_at, finished_at, notes). It aggregates validation_issue counts for that batch (errors and infos) and takes MAX(created_at) as last_validation. It attaches the previous batch (id, status, finished_at) for comparison. It returns null when no batch exists. Both /v1/acceptance and /v1/batches/latest use it.","tags":["domain:data-quality","entity:load-batch","entity:validation-issue"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_load","type":"card","group":"group_ingest","data":{"title":"CSV Load CLI (scripts/load.js)","description":"This script loads the data/geodb-v2/csv datasets into MySQL via lib/loader.loadAll(), in TABLE_ORDER for foreign-key safety (country first). Each run creates a load_batch record that tracks status, rows_loaded and start/end timestamps. After loading it prints COUNT(*) for every table. It then runs a Bogotá axis sanity check (ST_Latitude/ST_Longitude of geo_municipality 11001) to confirm points were not stored with swapped lat/lon. On failure it reports the batch id and exits with code 1. Data engineers use it to refresh the market-intelligence dataset.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","tech:csv-parse","tech:mysql8","role:data-engineer","entity:load_batch","flow:data-load"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/load.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_map_data","type":"card","group":"group_market_intel","data":{"title":"Map Data Layer (lib/mapData.js)","description":"Read-only (rule_map_api_readonly, SELECT-only) data layer that powers the market-intelligence map for tech talent and demand in Colombia. It serves three layers: (1) Departments – GeoJSON FeatureCollection from geo_department_shape with indicators: personas (employed in the 13 tech personas, optionally filtered by persona), core IT (ring='core'), micro-businesses, students 9–11, higher-ed on campus, SECOP software public procurement value (COP bn) and contracts 2025, Saber 11 computer-at-home %, developer and AI job vacancies; (2) Cities – municipality points (excluding 27493 and 'Rest of the country') with students, persona employment by metro area, active IT companies by chamber seat, Meetup members, and 2026 tech events list; (3) Bogotá localidades – polygons with EM2021 personas13, per 1,000 employed, core IT, software/IT companies (excluding BOG-00), household computer %. Each indicator carries table, column, unit and meta_sources source/year (cached) for traceability. Also exposes getPersonas() and getHealth() (MySQL version + Bogotá axis check). Unknown persona → 400. GeoJSON returned exactly as stored ([lon, lat]). Attribution: OpenStreetMap, DANE, Catastro Bogotá.","tags":["domain:market-intelligence","role:analyst","role:sales","entity:department","entity:municipality","entity:localidad","entity:persona","flow:map-exploration","tech:geojson","integration:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_companies_chamber","type":"table","group":"group_business_demand","data":{"name":"fact_companies_chamber","columns":[{"name":"chamber","type":"text","pk":true},{"name":"seat_municipality_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"department_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"businesses_renewed","type":"bigint"},{"name":"shops_4711_renewed","type":"bigint"},{"name":"it_companies_active","type":"bigint"}],"description":"Formal businesses per chamber of commerce from RUES (datos.gov.co c82u-588k): renewed registration in 2025/2026 excluding non-profits and cooperatives, neighbourhood shops (ISIC 4711) and active IT companies (ISIC 6201–6312). Chambers are placed at their seat municipality via an own mapping. 58 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_schools_municipality","type":"table","group":"group_education_pipeline","data":{"name":"fact_schools_municipality","columns":[{"name":"municipality_code","type":"CHAR(5)","pk":true,"fk":"geo_municipality.municipality_code"},{"name":"department_code","type":"CHAR(2)"},{"name":"students_9_11","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_g9","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_g10","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_g11","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_public","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_rural","type":"INT"},{"name":"schools","type":"INT"},{"name":"schools_public","type":"INT"},{"name":"reach_cap100","type":"INT"}],"description":"Secondary schools offering grades 9-11 and their students per municipality (MEN enrolment 2025). Business rule reach_cap100 = students reachable if a programme engages at most 100 students per school — a realistic outreach-capacity metric for school/edtech/talent-pipeline campaigns (Bogotá: 239,606 students, 1,087 schools, reach 93,898).","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_schools_municipality.csv","data/geodb-v2/csv/meta_sources.csv"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_load_batch","type":"table","group":"group_dq","data":{"name":"load_batch","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"INT","pk":true},{"name":"source_file","type":"VARCHAR(255)"},{"name":"status","type":"ENUM('running','validated','failed')"},{"name":"rows_loaded","type":"INT"},{"name":"started_at","type":"DATETIME"},{"name":"finished_at","type":"DATETIME NULL"},{"name":"notes","type":"TEXT"}],"description":"Audit record of each ingestion run. State machine: running → validated (all checks pass) | failed. Tracks rows loaded and timings; indexed by status so the acceptance panel can show the latest validated batch.","sourceFiles":["db/schema.sql"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_acceptance","type":"api","group":"group_governance","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/v1/acceptance","description":"Returns the acceptance panel for display in the UI: passed, total, all_green, axis_test{ok,...} and checks[]. Each check has group (v1/v2), table, label, expected and actual. Every check must expose expected and actual.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ passed, total, all_green, axis_test:{ok}, checks:[{group,table,label,expected,actual,ok}] }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-v1.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/probe-boot.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_em2021_localidad","type":"table","group":"group_bogota_em2021","data":{"name":"fact_em2021_localidad","columns":[{"name":"zone_id","type":"VARCHAR","pk":true,"fk":"geo_zone.zone_id"},{"name":"localidad","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"population","type":"INT"},{"name":"employed","type":"INT"},{"name":"personas13","type":"INT"},{"name":"core_it","type":"INT"},{"name":"personas13_per_1000_employed","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"core_it_per_1000_employed","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"hh_computer_pct","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"hh_internet_pct","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"telework_pct_of_employed","type":"DECIMAL"}],"description":"Bogotá Multipurpose Survey 2021 aggregated to the 20 localidades: population, employed, residents in the 13 personas and in core IT, densities per 1,000 employed, household computer/internet and telework rates. Powers the 'Bogotá por localidad' map layer and the localidad compare level. Business rule: not broken down by persona, so the persona filter is disabled for this layer (UI warns 'filtro por persona no disponible'). Chapinero/Teusaquillo are the densest knowledge-worker hubs; Suba has the largest absolute count.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_em2021_localidad.csv","public/js/map_view.js","public/js/compare_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_higher_ed_municipality","type":"table","group":"group_education_pipeline","data":{"name":"fact_higher_ed_municipality","columns":[{"name":"municipality_code","type":"CHAR(5)","pk":true,"fk":"geo_municipality.municipality_code"},{"name":"department_code","type":"CHAR(2)"},{"name":"students_total","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_on_campus","type":"INT"},{"name":"students_ict_field","type":"INT"}],"description":"Higher-education enrolment (SNIES 2024-2) by municipality where the programme is offered, with ICT-field students. Business rule: online programmes are attributed to the institution's HQ, inflating totals (e.g. Bogotá 863k total vs 454k on campus) — use students_on_campus for genuine local presence. Indicates the future ICT talent supply per city (Bogotá 113,672 ICT students).","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_higher_ed_municipality.csv","data/geodb-v2/csv/meta_sources.csv"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_validate","type":"api","group":"group_governance","data":{"method":"POST","path":"/v1/validate","description":"Triggers validation of the latest load batch, the same logic as the acceptance CLI. Validation persists issues and updates the batch status.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"validation summary"},"auth":"none (no auth — governance action exposed publicly in demo)","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_compare","type":"card","group":"group_market_intel","data":{"title":"Place Comparison Service (lib/compare.js)","description":"SELECT-only service for comparing 2–4 places side by side (rule_compare_same_level). Levels: department (Departamentos), municipality (Ciudades, with parent department), localidad (Localidades de Bogotá, zone_type='localidad', 11001). listPlaces(level) returns the catalog for selectors. compare({level, ids, persona}) parses comma-separated ids (deduplicated), enforces 2–4 places all belonging to the chosen level, then reuses mapData indicator functions so the comparison shows exactly the same indicators, values and source/year as the map. Persona filter applies to department and municipality levels; for localidades a note explains it does not apply (EM2021 source). Missing values → null (n.a.), e.g. 27493 has no geography. Errors: 400 for invalid level, wrong count, or places from another level. Response: {level, level_label, persona, persona_note, places[], indicators[{key,label,unit,table,column,source,values[]}], note}.","tags":["domain:market-intelligence","role:analyst","role:sales","entity:department","entity:municipality","entity:localidad","flow:compare-places","integration:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["lib/compare.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_companies_zone","type":"table","group":"group_business_demand","data":{"name":"fact_companies_zone","columns":[{"name":"zone_id","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"zone_name","type":"text"},{"name":"companies_total","type":"bigint"},{"name":"micro","type":"bigint"},{"name":"medium_large","type":"bigint"},{"name":"software_it","type":"bigint"},{"name":"design","type":"bigint"},{"name":"accounting_audit","type":"bigint"},{"name":"management_consulting","type":"bigint"},{"name":"research_market_studies","type":"bigint"},{"name":"higher_education_training","type":"bigint"},{"name":"shops_4711","type":"bigint"},{"name":"private_schools","type":"bigint"}],"description":"Registered companies by intra-city zone: Bogotá (March 2026, active & renewed, size by assets; SDDE/CCB) and Medellín (2022, no size breakdown; datos.gov.co pb3w-3vmc). Professional-services verticals (software, design, accounting, consulting, research, training, shops, private schools) indicate B2B buyer density. BOG-00 = companies with no localidad recorded. Mixed vintages must be footnoted in comparisons. 41 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_saber11_department","type":"table","group":"group_education_pipeline","data":{"name":"fact_saber11_department","columns":[{"name":"department_code","type":"CHAR(2)","pk":true,"fk":"geo_department.department_code"},{"name":"students_grade11","type":"INT"},{"name":"math_mean","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"global_mean","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"computer_at_home_pct","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"internet_at_home_pct","type":"DECIMAL"}],"description":"ICFES Saber 11 exam results per department: grade-11 test takers, mean math and global scores, and home computer/internet access. Measures quality and digital readiness of the future talent pool (Boyacá and Bogotá top math ~55; Chocó lowest 40.8).","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_saber11_department.csv"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_batches_latest","type":"api","group":"group_governance","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/v1/batches/latest","description":"Returns the most recent load_batch with status, rows_loaded, error count and info count, showing data freshness and quality.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ id, status, rows_loaded, errors, infos, ... }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-v1.js","scripts/probe-boot.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_em2021_upz","type":"table","group":"group_bogota_em2021","data":{"name":"fact_em2021_upz","columns":[{"name":"upz_code","type":"VARCHAR","pk":true},{"name":"upz_name","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"localidad_code","type":"CHAR(2)"},{"name":"reliable","type":"TINYINT"},{"name":"population","type":"INT"},{"name":"employed","type":"INT"},{"name":"personas13","type":"INT"},{"name":"core_it","type":"INT"},{"name":"personas13_per_1000_employed","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"core_it_per_1000_employed","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"hh_computer_pct","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"hh_internet_pct","type":"DECIMAL"},{"name":"telework_pct_of_employed","type":"DECIMAL"}],"description":"Same EM 2021 indicators at UPZ (planning-zone) granularity, the finest level in the DB, for neighbourhood targeting (e.g. Los Cedros 21,312 persona residents, La Floresta 56.4 core IT per 1,000). 8xx codes are merged UPZ groups (e.g. 'CHAPINERO: Pardo Rubio + Chapinero') to reach statistical reliability (reliable flag). Edge case: a row with upz_code 'NA' and empty name (localidad 20 Sumapaz rural) is a no-geography exception. Links to localidades via localidad_code → BOG-xx.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_em2021_upz.csv"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_micro_department","type":"table","group":"group_business_demand","data":{"name":"fact_micro_department","columns":[{"name":"department_code","type":"text","pk":true},{"name":"department","type":"text"},{"name":"micro_businesses","type":"bigint"}],"description":"Micro-businesses (≤9 people, formal and informal) by department, DANE EMICRON 2024. Only 24 departments + Bogotá are covered (25 rows) — remaining departments must show 'no data', not zero.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_map_view","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Mapa — geo market map (map_view.js)","description":"Primary analyst view: a Leaflet map of Colombia with three layer groups — Departamentos (choropleth polygons), Ciudades (proportional circle markers, radius ∝ sqrt(value/max), 2.5–26 px, large circles drawn first so small stay clickable) and Bogotá por localidad (choropleth). Indicators per group come from the API with table/column provenance shown under each option. Business rules: rule_quintile_legend — values are classed into 5 quintiles on a blue ramp with grey for no data; persona filter (13 personas with ring) re-queries dept and city layers and is unavailable for Bogotá localidades; contracts_2025 and tech_events hidden from selector (place card only); municipality 27493 without point excluded; cities hosting 2026 tech events get an orange ring. Hover/selected styles, tooltips with formatted values (%, miles de millones), dynamic source attribution, fitBounds on Bogotá. Stale-request guarding via S.seq; errors show an overlay message.","tags":["domain:geo-visualization","role:analyst","role:sales","tech:leaflet","entity:persona","entity:department","entity:municipality","entity:zone","flow:explore-map"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/map_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_issues","type":"api","group":"group_governance","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/v1/issues","description":"Lists validation issues for the batch, filtered by severity (e.g. 'info' returns the approved exceptions). An invalid severity value returns 400.","params":[{"name":"severity","type":"error|info|...","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ counts, issues:[...] } | 400 on invalid severity"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_vacancies_department","type":"table","group":"group_tech_ecosystem","data":{"name":"fact_vacancies_department","columns":[{"name":"keyword","type":"VARCHAR"},{"name":"department_code","type":"CHAR(2)","fk":"geo_department.department_code"},{"name":"offers","type":"INT"}],"description":"Job offers per Spanish search keyword (desarrollador, programador, ingeniero de sistemas, analista de datos, científico de datos, inteligencia artificial, soporte técnico, diseñador gráfico, marketing digital, contador, analista de negocio, auxiliar contable) per department. A live hiring-demand signal that maps to the personas (e.g. 'desarrollador' ↔ Software developers). Bogotá and Antioquia dominate; soporte técnico and auxiliar contable are highest volume.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/csv/fact_vacancies_department.csv"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_micro_national","type":"table","group":"group_business_demand","data":{"name":"fact_micro_national","columns":[{"name":"dimension","type":"text"},{"name":"category","type":"text"},{"name":"micro_businesses","type":"bigint"},{"name":"pct","type":"double precision"}],"description":"National distributions of micro-businesses across dimensions (activity, formality, technology use, place of operation, owner). Non-geographic long-format table (79 rows) used to size SMB/software-adoption opportunity.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_compare_view","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Comparar — side-by-side place comparison (compare_view.js)","description":"Lets a user pick 2 to 4 places of the same level (Departamentos, Ciudades, Localidades de Bogotá) and see all indicators in a table with source/year, best value highlighted per row (only when >1 non-null and max≠0), a summary strip with the first indicator, and CSV export (UTF-8 BOM, quoted, 'n.a.' for nulls, note appended). Defaults to Bogotá (11) vs Antioquia (05). Accent-insensitive search over name/code/parent (max 200 options shown); options disabled when 4 are chosen. Persona filter applies to fact_persona_* indicators and is disabled for localidades. Validation: fewer than 2 places → 'Selección incompleta' warning; API errors → danger alert. Place counts per level loaded in background.","tags":["domain:benchmarking","role:analyst","role:sales","flow:compare-places","entity:department","entity:municipality","entity:zone","tech:csv-export"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/compare_view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_load","type":"api","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"method":"POST","path":"/v1/load","description":"Full ETL reload. lib/loader.loadAll is lazy-required and re-imports the 27 source CSVs (parsed with csv-parse) into MySQL. This creates a new load_batch, after which validation runs automatically. The response contains the per-table report, the validation summary and the last 60 log lines. It is the destructive and expensive operation of the API. It is guarded by the busy mutex and has no authentication.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ batch_id, rows_loaded, tables, validation{status,errors,infos,passed,total}|null, log[≤60] }; 409 if busy; 500 on loader failure"},"auth":"none (should be restricted in production)","sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_facts","type":"table","group":"group_ingest","data":{"name":"fact_* / meta_sources","columns":[{"name":"fact_companies_zone","type":"table"},{"name":"fact_persona_metro","type":"table"},{"name":"fact_ict_by_sector","type":"table (sin geografía)"},{"name":"meta_sources","type":"source_name, year per table"}],"description":"Fact tables hold the market indicators: companies per zone, talent personas per metro area (including a 'Rest' bucket), and ICT by sector (a non-geographic table). meta_sources stores the source name and year for each dataset, so every number in the UI is traceable. The acceptance check reports any table missing a source or year. In total the explorer expects 27 fact_/geo_ tables.","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-tables.js","scripts/acceptance.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/smoke-extra.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_secop_department","type":"table","group":"group_business_demand","data":{"name":"fact_secop_department","columns":[{"name":"department_code","type":"text","pk":true},{"name":"contracts_2025","type":"bigint"},{"name":"value_cop_2025","type":"bigint"}],"description":"v2: public-sector contracts for software and IT services signed in 2025, by department of the buying entity (SECOP II, datos.gov.co jbjy-vk9h). Measures government as a software buyer: number of contracts and total value in COP. 32 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_tables","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"v1/tables","description":"Catalog of DB tables joined with meta_sources and geography detection.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ totals{tables,with_source_year,rows,sources,no_geo,with_geo}, tables[{table_name,rows,source_name,year,has_geo,geo_columns[],geo_level,kind}] }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/table_explorer.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_v1_table_rows","type":"api","group":"group_backend_api","data":{"method":"GET","path":"v1/tables/:table/rows","description":"Paginated (page_size 25) row preview of one table with optional LIKE search on text columns; geometry rendered via ST_AsText and long text truncated; rows flagged as approved geography exceptions. Table name must be whitelisted against the catalog (SQL-injection guard).","params":[{"name":"table","type":"path string","required":true},{"name":"page","type":"int","required":false},{"name":"q","type":"string","required":false}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ table,total,page,pages,page_size,q,columns[{name,type,kind}],rows[{...,__is_exception,__exception_reason}],has_geo,geo_level,geo_columns,truncated_columns,search_columns,exceptions_on_page,note }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["public/js/table_explorer.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_compare_places","type":"note","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"text":"**Flow: Compare candidate markets**\n1. Analyst chooses geographic level (department / city / zone)\n2. Searches & selects places from list (chips appear; places w/o data are disabled)\n3. Count hint warns when selection is below minimum (is-low)\n4. Summary cards show headline figure per place (grid uses --cols)\n5. Comparison table lists indicators × places, highlights best value per row, shows source per indicator\n6. Alerts/footnotes explain mixed vintages or aggregation; actions allow export/share\n\n**Data:** all fact tables via DIVIPOLA/zone keys, meta_sources\n**Edge cases:** empty selection → empty-table state; hidden alert when no issues","color":"#FDEDEC","sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/compare_view.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_lib_acceptance","type":"card","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"title":"lib/acceptance — Acceptance Rule Engine","description":"Read-only engine that evaluates the dataset acceptance criteria. Its checks cover the axis test (coordinate order), department polygon validity, unjoined codes across join columns (DANE code referential integrity), missing sources and documented exceptions. It returns checks, passed/total and accepted (all_green). The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from routes/v1.js.","tags":["domain:data-quality","entity:acceptance-check","rule:acceptance-criteria"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"note_business_rules","type":"note","group":"group_ingest","data":{"text":"**Core Geo Business Rules**\n- DIVIPOLA codes are always zero-padded strings: department 2 digits, municipality 5 digits. They are never numbers.\n- Spatial data uses SRID 4326. The DB axis order is lat/lon (Bogotá about 4.6 / -74.1), while GeoJSON output is [lon,lat] (lon in -82..-60, lat in -5..14).\n- There are 33 departments, 20 Bogotá localidades and 13 personas. Maps show at least 1000 municipalities.\n- 27493 is an approved no_geography_exception (info severity), never shown on the map.\n- Every indicator must cite source_name and year from meta_sources.\n- Raw table, column and code names are never translated (CSS .raw-name).","color":"#FDF2DC","sourceFiles":["scripts/migrate.js","scripts/check-map.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/acceptance.js","public/css/global.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_governance","type":"group","data":{"label":"Data Quality, Acceptance & Table Explorer (v1)","icon":"fa-solid fa-clipboard-check","color":"#F4ECF7","borderColor":"#7D3C98","sourceFiles":["scripts/acceptance.js","scripts/check-v1.js","scripts/check-tables.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_lib_validation","type":"card","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"title":"lib/validation — Batch Validation (flow_validation)","description":"Validates a load batch. It writes validation_issue rows with severity error or info, sets the batch status and reuses the acceptance computation (passed, total, axis.ok, accepted). Callers are POST /v1/validate and the loader after each reload. The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from routes/v1.js.","tags":["domain:data-quality","entity:validation-issue","entity:load-batch","flow:validation"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_lib_loader","type":"card","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"title":"lib/loader — CSV ETL Loader","description":"Reloads the 27 source CSVs (official Colombian statistics and geography) into MySQL. It records a load_batch, reports rows per table and triggers validation. It emits log messages through an injected log callback. The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from routes/v1.js.","tags":["domain:data-ingestion","integration:filesystem","tech:csv-parse","entity:load-batch","flow:data-reload"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_tables","type":"card","group":"group_catalog","data":{"title":"Table Catalog Service (lib/tables.js)","description":"Read-only catalog and paginated row preview for the Explorador de tablas, giving transparency into every table of the database with its source and year. listTables() builds a whitelist from information_schema (cached 60 s), classifies columns (geom, long, text, num), infers geographic level (Localidad/comuna, UPZ → localidad, Municipio, Departamento) and joins meta_sources for description/source/year; marks system tables (load_batch, validation_issue, meta_sources); returns totals (tables, registered, with source+year, rows, distinct sources, with/without geo). tableRows(table, page, q) validates the name (regex + catalog → 400/404), pages 25 rows ordered by PK, searches text columns with escaped bound LIKE parameters, truncates geometry (WKT long-lat, 90 chars) and long text (120), masks binaries, and flags approved exception rows with reasons (Rest of the country, BOG-00, 27493, Medellín without geometry). Tables without geo key get a note that they are excluded from Map and Compare. Security: identifiers only from information_schema, user input never interpolated.","tags":["domain:data-catalog","role:data-admin","role:analyst","entity:meta_sources","entity:table_catalog","flow:table-exploration","tech:information_schema","integration:mysql"],"sourceFiles":["lib/tables.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_developers_country","type":"table","group":"group_tech_ecosystem","data":{"name":"fact_developers_country","columns":[{"name":"iso2","type":"text","pk":true},{"name":"country","type":"text"},{"name":"developers","type":"bigint"},{"name":"developers_yoy_pct","type":"double precision"},{"name":"organizations","type":"bigint"},{"name":"organizations_yoy_pct","type":"double precision"},{"name":"pushes_per_dev","type":"double precision"},{"name":"enterprise_lang_share_pct","type":"double precision"}],"description":"GitHub developers and organisations per Latin American country, Q1 2026 (GitHub Innovation Graph). Benchmarks Colombia against LATAM peers on developer base, growth, activity and enterprise-language share. 18 rows, country-level (no DIVIPOLA key).","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_lib_tables","type":"card","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"title":"lib/tables — Table Catalogue & Row Browser","description":"Provides listTables (row counts, meta_sources provenance, has_geo) and tableRows (25-row pagination, search, whitelisted table names). It is the safe generic data browser behind the Table Explorer. The file was not analyzed directly; its contract is inferred from routes/v1.js.","tags":["domain:data-provenance","entity:meta-source","security:whitelist"],"sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_acceptance_cli","type":"card","group":"group_governance","data":{"title":"Acceptance Panel CLI (scripts/acceptance.js)","description":"This script runs lib/validation.validateBatch on the latest or a given load_batch and prints a Spanish 'PANEL DE ACEPTACIÓN'. Checks are grouped as v1 TOTALES DE CARGA (expected vs actual row totals with a tolerance) and v2 INTEGRIDAD GEOGRÁFICA. Each check shows expected, actual, difference and tolerance, and may list sub-checks (e.g. a máx/persona cap, offending codes). It also runs the Bogotá axis test (rule_axis_order), which compares the expected lat/lon ± tolerance with the actual SRID point. It lists approved info-level exceptions (no_geography_exception) and tables missing source or year in meta_sources. Finally it writes the batch status and prints passed/total, the error count and the exception count. Numbers use '.' as the thousands separator (es-CO).","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-engineer","role:auditor","entity:load_batch","entity:validation_issue","flow:acceptance"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/acceptance.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_dev_communities","type":"table","group":"group_tech_ecosystem","data":{"name":"fact_dev_communities","columns":[{"name":"municipality_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"city","type":"text"},{"name":"platform","type":"text"},{"name":"name","type":"text"},{"name":"members","type":"bigint"},{"name":"topic","type":"text"}],"description":"v2: technology Meetup groups with 300+ lifetime members per city (meetup.com search, 2026-10-02). Identifies community channels for developer marketing. 44 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_table_explorer","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Explorador de tablas — data catalog (table_explorer.js)","description":"Transparency/browsing page for data analysts: lists every DB table with row count, source and year from meta_sources, and geography status (geo column + level, or 'sin geografía' / 'sistema'). Stats cards: tables, rows, sources, no-geo tables (excluded from Map and Compare). Tabs filter all / with geo / without geo; client-side search; 25-row pagination. Opening a table loads a server-paginated preview with debounced (300 ms) LIKE search across text columns, column types, geometry shown as ST_AsText (truncated), NULL markers, and per-row exception flags (__is_exception with reason, e.g. 'Rest of the country' without code). Page CSV download includes a sin_geografia column. Keyboard: '/' focuses search, Enter/Space opens a row.","tags":["domain:data-catalog","role:data-analyst","role:admin","flow:browse-tables","entity:meta_sources","tech:pagination"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/table_explorer.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_fact_tech_events","type":"table","group":"group_tech_ecosystem","data":{"name":"fact_tech_events","columns":[{"name":"municipality_code","type":"text","fk":true},{"name":"city","type":"text"},{"name":"name","type":"text"},{"name":"date_2026","type":"text"},{"name":"size","type":"text"}],"description":"v2: main technology and AI events in Colombia, 2026 editions (official sites and press). Shown on the map as city circles with an orange ring ('city-event' swatch) and as an event list in the place card. 6 rows.","sourceFiles":["data/geodb-v2/schema_postgres.sql","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md","public/css/pages/map_view.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_acceptance_review","type":"note","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"text":"**Flow: Dataset Acceptance Review**\n1. Data steward or client opens Panel de aceptación.\n2. App calls GET /v1/acceptance, which returns the checks, axis test, polygon validity, missing sources, latest batch and all_green.\n3. When checks fail, the steward drills in with GET /v1/issues?severity=error.\n4. After fixes, the steward clicks re-validate (POST /v1/validate) and the panel refreshes.\n5. all_green=true means the dataset is accepted.\n\n**Roles:** Data steward, client reviewer\n**Data:** load_batch, validation_issue\n**Rules:** one write at a time (409); issue list capped at 500 rows; severity must be error or info (400)","color":"#fdebd0","sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js","public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_table_exploration","type":"note","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"text":"**Flow: Inspect a data table**\n1. User lands on Explorer; stat cards summarise catalogue\n2. Searches by name/source or switches tab (all / geo / non-geo)\n3. Clicks a table row (keyboard focusable) → row marked selected\n4. Preview shows meta (rows, source, geo level) and paginated rows\n5. NULLs shown italic; exception rows flagged with warning bar; footnote explains sample\n\n**Data:** meta_sources + any table from diccionario\n**Rules:** read-only; aggregated data only","color":"#FDEDEC","sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/table_explorer.css","data/geodb-v2/diccionario.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_data_reload","type":"note","group":"group_data_quality","data":{"text":"**Flow: Full Data Reload (ETL)**\n1. Steward triggers POST /v1/load.\n2. If busy is set, the call returns 409 'Operación en curso'. Otherwise busy='load'.\n3. loader.loadAll parses the 27 CSVs, loads the MySQL tables and creates a new load_batch.\n4. Validation runs automatically and writes validation_issue rows.\n5. The response carries batch_id, rows_loaded, the per-table report, the validation summary and the last 60 log lines.\n6. busy is cleared in finally, whether the run succeeded or failed.\n\n**State:** a new load_batch is created and its status is set by validation; the previous batch remains available as 'previous'\n**Risk:** unauthenticated destructive endpoint; the mutex lives in process memory only","color":"#fdebd0","sourceFiles":["routes/v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_validation_issue","type":"table","group":"group_dq","data":{"name":"validation_issue","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"INT","pk":true},{"name":"batch_id","type":"INT","fk":"load_batch.id"},{"name":"issue_type","type":"ENUM('unjoined_code','count_mismatch','total_mismatch','missing_source','no_geography_exception')"},{"name":"severity","type":"ENUM('error','info')"},{"name":"table_name","type":"VARCHAR(64)"},{"name":"column_name","type":"VARCHAR(64)"},{"name":"code_value","type":"VARCHAR(64)"},{"name":"expected_value","type":"VARCHAR(64)"},{"name":"actual_value","type":"VARCHAR(64)"},{"name":"message","type":"TEXT"},{"name":"created_at","type":"DATETIME"}],"description":"Data-quality findings per load batch (only enforced FK in schema, ON DELETE CASCADE). Types: unjoined_code (fact code not in geo tables), count_mismatch (row counts vs expected), total_mismatch (aggregates vs published totals), missing_source (no meta_sources entry), no_geography_exception (approved exceptions such as BOG-00, Nuevo Belén de Bajirá, Medellín comunas without geometry — severity info). Errors block 'validated' status.","sourceFiles":["db/schema.sql"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_acceptance","type":"note","group":"group_governance","data":{"text":"**Flow: Batch Acceptance & Data Governance**\n1. After a load, validateBatch runs (CLI or POST /v1/validate).\n2. v1 checks compare expected CSV totals with actual table counts within a tolerance.\n3. v2 checks test geographic integrity: FK codes, a per-persona maximum, and geometry presence.\n4. The axis test uses Bogotá 11001 (rule_axis_order).\n5. Approved exceptions (e.g. 27493 no_geography_exception) are recorded as info, not errors.\n6. load_batch.status is set; the UI reads /v1/acceptance, /v1/batches/latest and /v1/issues.\n\n**Roles:** data engineer, auditor, and the demo audience, who see a fully green panel as proof of data trustworthiness.","color":"#F4ECF7","sourceFiles":["scripts/acceptance.js","scripts/check-v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_table_explore","type":"note","group":"group_governance","data":{"text":"**Flow: Table Explorer**\n1. The user opens table_explorer from the sidebar.\n2. GET /v1/tables lists tables with row count, geo level (or 'sin geografía') and year.\n3. The user selects a table and searches (q), e.g. BOG or 05001.\n4. GET /v1/tables/:t/rows returns paginated rows; exception rows are highlighted with a reason.\n5. Raw names and codes are displayed untranslated in monospace.\n\n**Security:** table whitelist and parameterized search.","color":"#F4ECF7","sourceFiles":["scripts/check-tables.js","scripts/smoke.js","scripts/smoke-extra.js","public/css/global.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_qa","type":"group","data":{"label":"QA, Smoke & Deployment Verification","icon":"fa-solid fa-vial-circle-check","color":"#FDEDEC","borderColor":"#C2382F","sourceFiles":["scripts/smoke.js","scripts/probe-boot.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ui_map_view","type":"card","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"title":"Map View page (Mapa) — map_view.css","description":"Styles for the main geographic exploration page: a sticky left control panel plus a full-height Leaflet map. Panel sections: brand block, layer selector (radio options with active orange left rule and raw table/column name), persona filter with explanatory/warning notes, legend (5-class sequential blue choropleth r1–r5, grey 'no data', proportional city-circle sizes, orange-ringed circles for cities with tech events), place jump selector and a place card with indicator table, active-indicator highlight, event list and actions. Map overlays show the current layer title/meta, a geo-coverage warning note (e.g. missing geometry or partial coverage) and a loading state. Responsive: below 768px the panel stacks above a 62vh map. Users: market analysts/sales strategists deciding where in Colombia to focus.","tags":["domain:market-intelligence","domain:geospatial","role:analyst","flow:map-exploration","tech:css","tech:leaflet","entity:geo_department_shape","entity:geo_municipality","entity:fact_persona_department"],"sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/map_view.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_cdn_libs","type":"card","group":"group_frontend_shell","data":{"title":"External CDN Dependencies","description":"The frontend loads its third-party assets from CDNs: Bootstrap 5.3.3 (CSS and bundle JS from jsdelivr), Leaflet 1.9.4 for maps (unpkg), Font Awesome 6.5.2 (cdnjs) and Google Fonts (Inter, Manrope). The app therefore needs internet access to render correctly. No Subresource Integrity hashes are set; crossorigin is set, but integrity is not.","tags":["integration:cdn","tech:bootstrap","tech:leaflet","security:no-sri"],"sourceFiles":["public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_validation_acceptance","type":"note","group":"group_dq","data":{"text":"**Flow: Data Validation & Acceptance**\n1. Batch opened in load_batch (status=running)\n2. Each fact table's DIVIPOLA/zone codes checked against geo_department / geo_municipality / geo_zone → unjoined_code\n3. Row counts and totals compared to expected references → count_mismatch / total_mismatch\n4. Every table must have meta_sources row → missing_source\n5. Approved exceptions logged as severity=info no_geography_exception (BOG-00, 27493 NULL point, Medellín comunas no geometry, 'Rest of the country' NULL codes)\n6. Zero errors → status=validated, else failed\n7. Acceptance Panel page displays batch status and issues to reviewers\n\n**Roles:** Data engineer, reviewer/stakeholder (demo acceptance)\n**Entities:** load_batch, validation_issue, meta_sources","color":"#d5f5e3","sourceFiles":["db/schema.sql","public/js/pages/acceptance_panel.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_smoke","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"End-to-End Smoke Test (scripts/smoke.js)","description":"A 10-check HTTP test against the running service, targeting PROBE_PORT, argv or the default 45051. It verifies:\n1. Health: axis OK and MySQL >= 8.\n2. 33 department features with [lon,lat] inside Colombia's bounds and source/year present.\n3. The persona filter changes values.\n4. Municipalities exclude 27493 and include events.\n5. 20 localidades.\n6. Compare: 2 departments → 200; 1 place → 400; mixed levels → 400.\n7. Acceptance checks expose expected and actual.\n8. 27 tables with rows and year.\n9. geo_municipality rows return zero-padded string codes.\n10. index.html contains the sidebar and links to compare_view and table_explorer, and the map_view page and JS are served.\nThis is the demo-readiness gate.","tags":["domain:qa","tech:http","role:operator","flow:deploy-verify"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/smoke.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_smoke_extra","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"Extra Smoke (scripts/smoke-extra.js)","description":"Targeted regression checks:\n- Searching geo_municipality for 05001 (Medellín) must return department_code '05', confirming the leading zero is kept.\n- It prints a sample of localidad properties.\n- It prints the reported year of fact_companies_zone.","tags":["domain:qa","entity:divipola-code","role:operator"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/smoke-extra.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_app_shell","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"App shell & router (app.js)","description":"Single-page shell for the think4ever Geo DB Colombia app. Hash-based router load_page(id) supports 4 pages (map_view 'Mapa' default, compare_view 'Comparar', acceptance_panel 'Panel de aceptación', table_explorer 'Explorador de tablas'): it destroys the previous page (e.g. tears down Leaflet), fetches pages/{id}.html, swaps css/pages/{id}.css, lazily loads js/pages/{id}.js once and calls registerPage init(root). A loadSeq counter discards stale loads on fast navigation; failures render a Spanish empty-state error. Exposes the shared T4E helper: es-CO number formatting (fmt with 0/1/2 decimals, '—' for null), HTML escaping (esc, XSS protection for all rendered data), api() fetch wrapper that throws on non-2xx with truncated body, and isDark(). Light/dark theme persisted in localStorage 't4e-theme' and broadcast as 't4e:theme' event. All URLs are relative because the app runs behind /run/<projectId>/.","tags":["domain:ui-shell","tech:vanilla-js","tech:spa-router","role:analyst","security:xss-escape"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_fact_tables","type":"card","group":"group_geo_model","data":{"title":"Fact tables (market indicators)","description":"Aggregated indicator tables joined to geography by DIVIPOLA/zone codes: persona breakdowns (fact_persona_metro, _department, _segment; 'Rest of the country' rows have NULL municipality), fact_ict_by_sector, education (fact_schools_municipality 11,111 schools / 1.73M students 9–11, fact_higher_ed_municipality 2.56M enrolment, fact_saber11_department computer_at_home_pct), business (fact_micro_department 5.26M, fact_micro_national, fact_companies_chamber it_companies_active by seat municipality, fact_companies_zone Bogotá/Medellín with BOG-00 exception), demand (fact_secop_department contracts/value 2025, fact_vacancies_department offers by keyword 'desarrollador'/'inteligencia artificial'), ecosystem (fact_developers_country, fact_dev_communities Meetup members, fact_tech_events 2026), Bogotá survey (fact_em2021_localidad, fact_em2021_upz). All aggregates — no personal data.","tags":["domain:market-intelligence","entity:fact","integration:dane","integration:icfes","integration:secop","integration:meetup"],"sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js","lib/acceptance.js","lib/mapData.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_loader_batch","from":"node_loader","to":"tbl_load_batch","label":"opens and closes load batch","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_probe_boot","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"Boot Probe (scripts/probe-boot.js)","description":"A one-shot post-deploy probe. It calls /, /health, /v1/acceptance, /v1/tables, /v1/batches/latest and /api/map/departments with a 15 s timeout, and any 5xx or connection error fails the probe. It then connects directly to MySQL using the DB_* environment variables and counts geo_municipality rows to confirm data exists.","tags":["domain:qa","integration:mysql","role:operator","flow:deploy-verify"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/probe-boot.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_router_shim_pattern","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Page Router Shim Pattern","description":"The SPA shell loads js/pages/{id}.js for each route; each shim registers the page via window.registerPage(id, {init, destroy}) and lazily injects the real module script (js/{id}.js) on first navigation. Business benefit: fast initial load—heavy views (map, comparisons, table explorer) only download when the analyst opens them. Behaviour: memoised loading promise prevents duplicate script tags; if the global module (window.T4E*) already exists it resolves immediately; on script load failure the promise is reset (allowing retry) and rejects with a Spanish user-facing error 'No se pudo cargar js/...'. destroy() delegates to the module only if loaded, letting the shell tear down page state on route change. No auth logic client-side; all four pages are read-only analyst views.","tags":["domain:frontend","tech:vanilla-js","tech:lazy-loading","pattern:router-shim","role:analyst"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/pages/acceptance_panel.js","public/js/pages/compare_view.js","public/js/pages/map_view.js","public/js/pages/table_explorer.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_loader_geo","from":"node_loader","to":"tbl_geo_municipality","label":"loads geography with SRID 4326 points","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_loader_facts","from":"node_loader","to":"node_fact_tables","label":"replaces indicator data","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ui_compare_view","type":"card","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"title":"Compare View page (Comparar) — compare_view.css","description":"Styles for side-by-side comparison of selected places (departments/cities/zones). Left sticky panel: geographic level radio options with counts, searchable multi-select place list (aria-selected checkboxes, disabled options for places without data, DIVIPOLA code shown), removable chips and a count hint that turns warning-coloured when too few places are selected. Main area: summary cards per place (headline figure + classification), and a comparison table with sticky indicator column, numeric right-aligned cells, 'best' value marked with bold + navy underline, and a source column (from meta_sources). Includes alert banner, empty state, aggregation note and footnotes (e.g. differing vintages). Responsive to single column on mobile; honours reduced-motion.","tags":["domain:market-intelligence","role:analyst","role:sales-strategist","flow:compare-places","tech:css","tech:accessibility","entity:geo_department","entity:geo_municipality","entity:meta_sources"],"sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/compare_view.css"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_loader_meta","from":"node_loader","to":"tbl_meta_sources","label":"registers source and year","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_loader_validation","from":"node_loader","to":"node_validation","label":"triggers post-load validation","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/loader.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_check_map","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"Map Data Unit Check (scripts/check-map.js)","description":"Calls lib/mapData and lib/compare directly, without a server, and asserts:\n- health axis_check_ok.\n- 33 departments, all with geometry.\n- Every indicator has a source and year.\n- At least 1000 municipalities with lat/lon, and no 27493.\n- 20 localidades with geometry; the first coordinate is printed as [lon,lat].\n- 13 personas.\n- A Bogotá vs Antioquia compare table with values and sources (es-CO formatting).\n- The localidad compare works.\n- Invalid compare requests (one id, mixed level, unknown level 'x') return status 400.","tags":["domain:qa","domain:geo-map","role:developer"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/check-map.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_validation_acceptance","from":"node_validation","to":"node_acceptance","label":"computes acceptance checks","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/validation.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_page_acceptance_panel","type":"card","group":"group_frontend","data":{"title":"Acceptance Panel Page (acceptance_panel)","description":"Route shim for the data acceptance/QA dashboard; lazy-loads js/acceptance_panel.js exposing window.T4EAcceptancePanel. Business purpose: lets stakeholders and data engineers verify that the loaded Geo DB is trustworthy before demoing insights—surfacing load_batch status (running/validated/failed), validation_issue findings by type and severity, approved exceptions, and source coverage from meta_sources.","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:reviewer","role:data-engineer","entity:load_batch","entity:validation_issue","flow:acceptance"],"sourceFiles":["public/js/pages/acceptance_panel.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_validation_issue","from":"node_validation","to":"tbl_validation_issue","label":"records errors and exceptions","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/validation.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_validation_batch","from":"node_validation","to":"tbl_load_batch","label":"sets validated / failed","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/validation.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_acceptance_facts","from":"node_acceptance","to":"node_fact_tables","label":"verifies totals and joins","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/acceptance.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_check_map_view","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"Map View Static Check (scripts/check-map-view.js)","description":"Parses the map_view JS and its shim with the vm module and checks for required API calls, ramp colours, UI strings and functions. It fails if an absolute-URL fetch is found, because that would break behind the proxy. It verifies the HTML contract: map-panel, map-canvas, #map, radiogroup, aria-live, place-card and map-foot. It also executes the quintile logic in a sandbox via window.T4EMapView._computeQuintiles/_classOf to confirm class assignment and null handling.","tags":["domain:qa","tech:frontend","a11y","role:developer"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/check-map-view.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_acceptance_axis","from":"node_acceptance","to":"tbl_geo_municipality","label":"tests Bogotá axis order","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/acceptance.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_panel_validation","from":"node_acceptance_panel","to":"node_validation","label":"Revalidar reruns validation","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["public/pages/acceptance_panel.html","lib/validation.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_panel_acceptance","from":"node_acceptance_panel","to":"node_acceptance","label":"displays check results","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["public/pages/acceptance_panel.html"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_check_v1","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"v1 Router Check (scripts/check-v1.js)","description":"Mounts routes/v1 on an ephemeral port, separate from the service port, and exercises:\n- POST /v1/validate\n- GET /v1/acceptance (prints each check as OK/FALLA)\n- GET /v1/batches/latest\n- GET /v1/issues?severity=info\n- GET /v1/issues?severity=x, which must return 400.","tags":["domain:qa","domain:data-quality","role:developer"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/check-v1.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_panel_explorer","from":"node_acceptance_panel","to":"node_table_explorer","label":"navigates to catalog","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["public/pages/acceptance_panel.html","public/pages/table_explorer.html"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_compare_map","from":"node_compare","to":"node_map_data","label":"reuses map indicators for consistency","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/compare.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_mapdata_facts","from":"node_map_data","to":"node_fact_tables","label":"aggregates indicators","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ui_table_explorer","type":"card","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"title":"Table Explorer page (Explorador de tablas) — table_explorer.css","description":"Styles for browsing the raw database catalog (UI design #1550), scoped under #exp-page so it works standalone. Stat cards (tables, rows, sources), search bar with keyboard shortcut hint, tab rail with counts to filter tables (e.g. geo vs non-geo), table list with selectable rows, geo-level badges (tag-geo in monospace with key level; tag-nogeo warning badge for tables lacking a geographic key, e.g. fact_ict_by_sector, fact_micro_national), and a data preview with paginated rows, null-value styling, exception rows marked with a warning bar (e.g. 'Rest of the country', BOG-00, unreliable UPZ) and sample/footer notes. Serves analysts and data engineers verifying what data exists and where it comes from.","tags":["domain:data-catalog","role:analyst","role:data-engineer","flow:table-exploration","tech:css","entity:meta_sources"],"sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/table_explorer.css"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_mapdata_shapes","from":"node_map_data","to":"tbl_geo_department_shape","label":"serves department polygons","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_check_tables","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"Table Explorer Check (scripts/check-tables.js)","description":"Exercises lib/tables directly. It lists the catalog, and pages and searches representative tables, printing exception rows and geometry samples. The cases are BOG-00 in fact_companies_zone, Rest in fact_persona_metro, 27493 in geo_municipality, geo_zone pages 1 and 2, and the non-geo fact_ict_by_sector. Security probes: a SQL-injection table name, an unknown table and a path traversal must all be rejected, and an injection-like search string must be treated as a literal.","tags":["domain:qa","security:sql-injection","role:developer"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/check-tables.js"]}}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_mapdata_zone","from":"node_map_data","to":"tbl_geo_zone","label":"serves Bogotá localidades","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_mapdata_meta","from":"node_map_data","to":"tbl_meta_sources","label":"cites source and year","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js"]}
{"cmd":"link","id":"link_mapdata_persona","from":"node_map_data","to":"tbl_fact_persona_profile","label":"filters by persona","toArrow":"arrow","sourceFiles":["lib/mapData.js"]}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_check_syntax","type":"card","group":"group_qa","data":{"title":"Syntax Check (scripts/check-syntax.js)","description":"A quick compile-only gate for the Table Explorer feature files (frontend JS, lib/tables.js, routes/v1.js). It also confirms that routes/v1 can be required without errors.","tags":["domain:qa","role:developer"],"sourceFiles":["scripts/check-syntax.js"]}}
