{"cmd":"add","id":"node_ui_acceptance_panel","type":"card","group":"group_ui_pages","data":{"title":"Acceptance Panel page (Panel de aceptación) — acceptance_panel.css","description":"Styles for the data-quality acceptance dashboard (UI design #1549) that validates the loaded database before it is used. Shows an overall verdict banner (pass = success, fail = danger) with run metadata, 4 KPI stat cards, a totals table of checks grouped by section (check, tolerance, state dot, sub-rows, total rows, failing rows tinted red), a two-column 'duo' with code blocks (e.g. the SQL/axis check) and definition lists, batch figures (3 headline numbers), and an issue list with severity pills, messages and raw-name metadata. Running state dims the table and spins the refresh icon (disabled for reduced motion). Used by data engineers/QA and the demo owner to certify that row counts and totals match the dictionary.","tags":["domain:data-quality","role:data-engineer","role:qa","flow:data-acceptance","tech:css","entity:meta_sources"],"sourceFiles":["public/css/pages/acceptance_panel.css"]}}
